# research-lit.manifest.result.json (Step 1)

**Single contract for Step 1** (manifest JSON shape + report rules). Wrapper `bash aris-constraints/research-lit.aris.example.sh` loads **only this `.desc` file**.

## Data anchor (mandatory when present)

If **`data-source/DATA_SOURCE_PROFILE.en.md`** exists, read it + **`data-source/data-source-discovery.manifest.result.json`** before search. §2 literature must **fit the locked primary dataset** (modalities, cohort, gaps) and cite **`### 2.1`** / stable ID. Full rules: **`aris-constraints/data-anchor.requirement.example.desc`**.

## Agent entry

1. Read `RESEARCH_BRIEF.md`. If data profile exists, read **`data-source/DATA_SOURCE_PROFILE.en.md`** (and `.zh.md` if helpful).
2. Follow **only this `.desc` file** (including **Example JSON**).
3. Write **`idea-stage/research-lit.manifest.result.json` only** (never `aris-constraints/research-lit.manifest.json` or other names). Edit **§2 and §6 only** inside existing `idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.en.md` / `.zh.md` — **do not** append a second literature chapter or replace the whole file. When profile exists, set **`data_anchor`** object in manifest (see data-anchor requirement).

## Delivery paths (do not swap)

| Artifact | Path | Wrong |
|----------|------|-------|
| Manifest JSON | **`idea-stage/research-lit.manifest.result.json`** | `aris-constraints/*.json`, symlinks |
| Composed report | **`idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.en.md`**, **`.zh.md`** | new files under `aris-constraints/` |

**Forbidden manifest keys** (not in Example JSON): `name`, `description`, `verification_status_summary` as top-level substitutes for `papers[]` / `report_path`.

## Example JSON (`idea-stage/research-lit.manifest.result.json`)

Replace example values; keep keys and nesting.

```json
{
  "aris_phase": "research-lit",
  "result": "success",
  "report_path": "idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.en.md",
  "zh_report_path": "idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.zh.md",
  "finished_at": "2026-10-19T12:00:00Z",
  "sources_used": ["arxiv", "web", "gemini"],
  "data_anchor": {
    "profile_en": "data-source/DATA_SOURCE_PROFILE.en.md",
    "discovery_manifest": "data-source/data-source-discovery.manifest.result.json",
    "primary_dataset_id": "d1",
    "primary_label": "OpenNeuro ds######"
  },
  "papers": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "title": "Example paper title",
      "year": 2021,
      "venue": "NeuroImage",
      "urls": [
        "https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.01351",
        "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuroimage.2021.117123"
      ],
      "doi": "10.1016/j.neuroimage.2021.117123",
      "arxiv_id": "2111.01351",
      "pmid": null,
      "pdf_path": null
    }
  ]
}
```

## ARIS runtime (from `research-lit.aris.example.sh`)

| Option | Value |
|--------|--------|
| skill | `/research-lit` |
| language | `en` |
| paper library | `literature/` |
| sources | `all`, `gemini` |
| ARXIV_DOWNLOAD | `false` |
| ARXIV_MAX_DOWNLOAD | `5` |
| composed | `idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.en.md`, `idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.zh.md` |

## result

**Delivery only** — not literature quality or coverage. Put assessment in the report prose, not in `result`.

- `"success"` — use when **all** of: valid JSON; non-empty `papers[]` with required fields per table below; composed report sections in **both** `idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.en.md` and `idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.zh.md` meet the template contract below (§2 and §6); each paper’s URL rule is met in the English report (see below).
- `"failed"` — only if Step 1 **could not complete** the contract (e.g. empty papers, missing report section). Still write the file.
- **Do not** use `"partial"` or other values.

## Top-level fields

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| aris_phase | `"research-lit"` |
| report_path | `"idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.en.md"` |
| zh_report_path | `"idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.zh.md"` (Simplified Chinese; same `sec-*` anchors as EN) |
| finished_at | UTC ISO-8601 |
| sources_used | string array (sources actually used, e.g. `web`, `arxiv`, `gemini`) |
| papers | non-empty array |

## papers[] (each entry)

| Field | Required for success |
|-------|----------------------|
| id | stable id, e.g. `p1`, `p2`, … |
| title | non-empty string |
| year | integer |
| venue | string (may be empty in edge cases; example shows filled) |
| urls | string array; **or** satisfy address rule via doi / arxiv_id |
| doi | string or null |
| arxiv_id | string or null |
| pmid | null or string |
| pdf_path | null or path under project |

**Address rule (each paper):** at least one of: non-empty `urls[]`, non-null `doi`, non-null `arxiv_id`.

## Composed reports (Step 1 owns §2 and §6)

**Section layout (read-only reference):**

- English: `aris-constraints/md_template/IDEA_REPORT.en.example.md`
- Chinese: `aris-constraints/md_template/IDEA_REPORT.zh.example.md`

After init, **`idea-stage/` holds the working reports** (same structure as the templates above):

| File | Language | Step 1 fills |
|------|----------|----------------|
| `idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.en.md` | English | **§2** Literature landscape, **§6** References |
| `idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.zh.md` | Simplified Chinese | **§2** 文献综述, **§6** 参考文献 |

### Edit scope (mandatory)

When editing `idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.en.md` and `idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.zh.md`:

- **Only change** Step 1 spans: **§2** (from `## Literature Landscape` / `## 文献综述` through the `---` before §3) and **§6** References / 参考文献 (including `sec-6` block).
- **Do not change** anything else: `#` title and intro blurb, `## Table of contents` / `## 目录`, **§1**, **§3–§5**, or any text outside §2 and §6.
- **Do not** delete, reorder, or rewrite headings outside §2/§6; **do not** replace or truncate the whole report file.

**Step 1:** use the `aris-constraints/md_template/*.example.md` files to see which subsections belong in §2 and §6; write content only inside those spans in both idea-stage files. Replace each `[…]` hint with real prose from `papers[]`. Keep contract H2s inside §2/§6 unchanged. Do not leave `[…]` placeholders in §2 or §6.

If files are missing, run `bash aris-constraints/all-init-project.example.sh` — normal workflow assumes init already ran.

For `result=success`:

- **English** (`IDEA_REPORT.en.md`) — H2 exactly:

      ## Literature Landscape

- **Chinese** (`IDEA_REPORT.zh.md`) — H2 exactly:

      ## 文献综述

Every `papers[]` entry must appear in §2.4 and §6; EN and ZH use the same papers and the same chosen URL per paper (verbatim).

### URL rule (validate uses English file)

For each paper, at least **one** string from `papers[].urls` MUST appear verbatim in `idea-stage/IDEA_REPORT.en.md` (not necessarily every URL in the array). Prefer the same URL in `IDEA_REPORT.zh.md` §2.4 and §6.
